  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "National Puppy Day is celebrated annually on March 23 to honor the magic puppies bring to our lives, promote the adoption of orphaned pups, and raise awareness about ending puppy mills. Founded in 2006 by Colleen Paige, this day encourages celebrating through adoption, volunteering at shelters, and pampering puppies. Key Aspects of National Puppy Day: Purpose: To celebrate the unconditional love of puppies and educate the public on the cruelty of puppy mills. Adoption Focus: It encourages people to rescue puppies from local shelters rather than purchasing from pet stores or irresponsible breeders. How to Celebrate: Adopt: Visit a local shelter to find a new furry family member. Volunteer/Donate: Support shelters with supplies like food, blankets, and toys. Pamper: Spend extra time playing, walking, or brushing your pup. Share: Post photos of your puppies on social media using #NationalPuppyDay. National Puppy Day 2026 is observed on March 23, 2026.",
